* regardless of \\( A \\).\n\n- **Relevance of other premises:**  \n  Premise 6\u2019s condition (well-attended weddings require July or Paris travel) is irrelevant because John cannot have a wedding in the first place. Similarly, the existence of well-attended July weddings (Premise 4) does not affect John\u2019s case.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion:\nJohn\u2019s inability to have a wedding (\u00acW) directly confirms that he cannot have a well-attended wedding. The statement is **true**. Therefore, the correct answer is:  \n**A) True**",
